  "answer": "I found no past ticket in the archive that reports this problem. The archive has older \"Settings doesn't open\" tickets, but they have different causes. One example is terminal#16960, where the Settings editor failed to launch because of a font-loading regression on Windows 10. None of them involve commit 58c0db9 (\"Add expander groups to settings UI (#20200)\"). This looks like a new regression in the current git branch. Please keep the ticket open as a new bug. Include your bisect result (the commit that introduced it) and any crash or event log output you can capture. Until a fix lands, you can work around it by building from the commit just before #20200, or by editing settings.json directly. You can open it with Ctrl+Shift+, or by Shift-clicking the Settings menu item."
